### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@authToken = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Root Health Check
GET http://localhost:5000/
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. User Registration (Mocks OTP to console logs)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Vaibhav",
  "identifier": "vaibhav@example.com"
}

### 3. User Login (Mocks OTP to console logs)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "vaibhav@example.com"
}

### 4. Verify OTP (Copy the 6-digit code logged to server console)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "vaibhav@example.com",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### 5. Add Loan Entry (friend name, amount, due date)
POST {{baseUrl}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "friend_name": "Rahul Sharma",
  "amount": 2500.00,
  "due_date": "2026-11-15",
  "notes": "Emergency loan for car repair"
}

### 6. Add Another Loan Entry (Overdue Example for summary)
POST {{baseUrl}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "friend_name": "Amit Kumar",
  "amount": 1000.00,
  "due_date": "2026-09-01",
  "notes": "Book purchase"
}

### 7. Get Loan Summary (total lent, total repaid, overdue amount)
GET {{baseUrl}}/loans/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 8. List All User Loans
GET {{baseUrl}}/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 9. Record Repayment Towards a Loan
POST {{baseUrl}}/loans/1/repay
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "amount": 1500.00
}
